# The RS-232 FujiNet User's Manual

Driving every FujiNet device through a plain serial port: setting up
`fnconfig.ini`, the FujiBus packet, a command reference for every device with
real byte streams, and three complete Z80 programs (CONFIG, NETCAT, 5 Card
Stud) for an Altair 8800 with an 88-2SIO. This is the wiki condensation; the
full illustrated edition, with every listing, is the PDF in `rs232/` of the
[manuals repository](https://github.com/FujiNetWIFI/fujinet-manuals/tree/main/rs232).

It describes `fujinet-firmware` at commit `670b2ed55`. Every byte stream
below was captured from a running adapter (`tools/examples.py`); where the
firmware does something unexpected, it says so, and
[Firmware behaviour and errata](#firmware-behaviour-and-errata) collects every
case with its source reference.

See also the [FujiNet-Network-Protocol-Handbook](FujiNet-Network-Protocol-Handbook)
for the network protocols themselves.

