`C1`, `A0`-`A9`, `90`, `3F`.

## The disk drives (31h-38h)

Extensions: `.IMD` ImageDisk; `.ROM .BIN .INT .ITV .CHF` cartridge ROM (**do
not mount** on a serial computer: the firmware pushes the ROM to device `FF`
and waits for replies); anything else a flat image of **512-byte** sectors.

| Code | Command | Params / payload | Reply |
|---|---|---|---|
| `52` | READ | p0 sector (32-bit) | 512 (NAK past the end or empty slot) |
| `57` / `50` | WRITE / PUT | p0 sector; 512 bytes | ACK (NAK if read-only) |
| `53` | STATUS | **do not use** - it is wired to WRITE | |
| `21` / `22` | FORMAT / FORMAT_MEDIUM | - | 128: `FF FF` 00... (image untouched) |
| `4E` / `4F` | PERCOM_READ / WRITE | - / 12 | 12 / ACK |

{{ex:disk.write}}

## The network units (71h-78h)

Devicespec: a URL with optional `N:` prefix, NUL-terminated, up to 255
characters. Protocols are covered in the Network Protocol Handbook.

| Code | Command | Params / payload | Reply |
|---|---|---|---|
| `4F` | OPEN | p0 mode, p1 translation; devicespec | ACK / NAK (STATUS says why) |
| `43` | CLOSE | - | ACK |
| `53` | STATUS | - | 4: waiting (16), connected, status |
| `52` | READ | p0 max (16) | up to p0 bytes; NAK if none |
| `57` | WRITE | p0 count (16); data | ACK |
| `FC` | SET_PARSER | p0 0, p1: 1 JSON, 2 HTML, 3 XML | ACK |
| `50` | PARSE | - | ACK |
| `51` | QUERY | path | ACK (then STATUS + READ) |
| `FB` | SET_PARAMETER | p0 0 flags / 1 EOL, p1 value | ACK |
| `54` | TRANSLATION | p0 0, p1 translation | ACK |
| `4C` | SET_EOL | EOL bytes | ACK |
| `5A` | SET_INT_RATE | p0 ms | ACK |
| `25` / `26` | SEEK / TELL | p0 offset (32) / - | ACK / 4 |
| `30` / `2C` | GETCWD / CHDIR | - / path | path (no NUL) / ACK |
| `FD` / `FE` | USERNAME / PASSWORD | NUL-terminated | ACK |
| `20` | RENAME | p0 mode, p1 0; `spec,new` NUL | ACK |
| `21` `23` `24` `2A` `2B` | DELETE LOCK UNLOCK MKDIR RMDIR | p0 mode, p1 0; spec NUL | ACK |
| `41` | ACCEPT | - | ACK |
| `63` | CLOSE_CLIENT | - | **inverted**: NAK after a disconnect |
| `4D` | SET_HTTP_MODE | p0 0, p1: 0 body, 1 collect headers, 2 get headers, 3 set headers, 4 POST data | ACK |
| `72` | GET_REMOTE | - | 256: `addr:port` ended by `9B` (NAK on ESP32) |
| `44` | SET_DESTINATION | `N:host:port` **and a NUL** | ACK |

Open modes: `04` read/GET, `05` DELETE, `06` directory, `07` directory alt,
`08` write/PUT, `09` append/DELETE+headers, `0C` read-write/GET+headers, `0D`
POST, `0E` PUT+headers. Translation: `00` none, `01` CR, `02` LF, `03` CR LF,
`04` PETSCII. **End of data:** TCP - nothing waiting and connected `00`; HTTP -
nothing waiting and status `88` (connected is `00` throughout). UDP on
fujinet-pc: STATUS never counts datagrams; READ anyway.

An HTTP GET:

{{ex:net.open_get}}
{{ex:net.status_get}}
{{ex:net.read}}
{{ex:net.status_eof}}

JSON (after OPEN): SET_PARSER, PARSE, QUERY, STATUS, READ:

{{ex:net.query}}
{{ex:net.status_q}}
{{ex:net.read_q}}

Status codes: 1 OK, 131 write-only, 132 invalid command, 135 read-only, 136
EOF, 138 timeout, 144 general, 146 not implemented, 151 exists, 162 no space,
165 bad devicespec, 166 bad position, 167 access denied, 170 not found, 200
refused, 201 unreachable, 202 socket timeout, 203 network down, 204 reset, 205
in progress, 206 address in use, 207 not connected, 208 server not running,
209 no connection waiting, 210 service unavailable, 211 aborted, 212 bad
login, 213 JSON parse, 214 client error, 215 server error, 255 no buffers.

## The clock (45h)

Every command takes p0 (`01` = alternate zone where honoured) - always send it.

| Code | Command | Reply |
|---|---|---|
| `93` | GETTIME | 6: day, month, year-2000, h, m, s |
| `9A` | GETTZTIME | 6, alternate zone |
| `54` | GET_SIMPLE (named SETTZ_ALT2; a read on RS-232) | 7: century, year, month, day, h, m, s |
| `4D` | GET_SIMPLE_HUNDREDTHS | 8 |
| `50` | GET_PRODOS | 4 |
| `53` | GET_SOS | `YYYYMMDD0HHMMSS000` NUL |
| `49` | GET_ISO_LOCAL | `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS+HHMM` NUL |
| `5A` | GET_ISO_UTC | the same, `+0000` |
| `47` / `4C` | GET_GENERAL / GETTZ_LEN | zone NUL / length+1 |
| `99` | SETTZ (payload zone NUL) | ACK - alternate zone, not saved |
| `74` | SETTZ_ALT (payload zone NUL) | ACK - system zone, saved |

{{ex:clock.iso_local}}

## The printer (40h)

WRITE/PUT (`57`/`50`): up to **255** bytes (longer is cut; over 320 overruns
the buffer). STATUS (`53`, p0 required): 4 bytes. Types (`[Printer1] type`):
0 raw file, 1 text file (default), 2 ASCII, 3-11 Atari models, 12 Epson 80,
13 Epson PrintShop, 14 Okimate 10, 15 PNG, 16 HTML, 17 HTML ATASCII.

{{ex:printer.write}}

## The modem (50h)

Raw text outside a frame (or a WRITE `57` payload) goes to the AT parser; the
modem's output, including its replies to FujiBus commands, is **raw and
unframed**. Immediate AT responses (`OK`, `ATIP`) are suppressed on RS-232;
`CONNECT` and `NO CARRIER` appear. `ATDThost:port` dials (port 23 default),
`ATH`/`+++ATH` hangs up, `ATPORTn` listens, `ATPBn=host:port` phonebook.
**`ATCPM` crashes the adapter.** STATUS (`53`, p0) returns 2 raw bytes.

## CP/M (5Ah)

Compiled in, never added to the bus: device `5A` answers like a missing
device. Run CP/M on the computer from a disk slot instead.

## The Z80 programs

Three include files in `listings/common/`: **ALTAIR.INC** (the only
hardware code: 88-2SIO port A `10h/11h` terminal, port B `12h/13h` FujiNet,
6850 reset `03h` then `15h`, RDRF bit 0, TDRE bit 1; routines between
`PLATFORM BEGIN`/`END` markers), **FUJIBUS.INC** (FBNEW, FBBYTE, FBWORD,
FBMEM, FBSTR, FBCALL with drain, retry and optional RESEND; FBERR 1-6) and
**CONIO.INC**. All programs are `ORG 0100h`, no BDOS calls; assemble with
`z88dk-z80asm -b` (`-DCPM=1` to exit to CP/M, `-DUSE_RESEND=1` for RESEND).

- **HELLO** - WiFi status and host slots.
- **CONFIG** (`listings/config/fncfg.asm`) - host slots (H), browse and mount
  (B), eject (E), WiFi (W), list (L), quit (Q); plain scrolling text.
- **NETCAT** (`listings/netcat/netcat.asm`) - OPEN mode 12, then WRITE keys,
  STATUS + READ to print; Ctrl-] hangs up.
- **5 CARD STUD** (`listings/5cs/stud.asm`) - HTTPS GETs to
  `5card.carr-designs.com` with `&bin=1` (fixed binary state: last result 81,
  round, pot, active player, move time, viewing, move count, 5 moves x 13,
  player count, players x 33); full table per round, one line per move,
  Teletype-friendly.

To port to other hardware, rewrite only the PLATFORM routines (examples for
an 8251 USART, a Z80 SIO and CP/M BIOS console calls are in the PDF).

## Running the examples in SIMH

AltairZ80 with `set m2sio0 enabled`, `set m2sio1 enabled`, `set m2sio0
noconsole`, **`set m2sio0 dtr` / `set m2sio1 dtr`** (connections wait for
DTR), **`deposit clock 2000`** (2 MHz, so the software timeouts hold),
`attach m2sio0 <port>;notelnet`, `attach m2sio1 <port>;notelnet`, then bridge
port B to fujinet-pc's BoIP port with `socat`. `sim/run.sh` and `sim/term.py`
in the manuals repo do all of this.

## Firmware behaviour and errata

| Command | Behaviour | Source |
|---|---|---|
| any | missing parameter: uncaught exception (crash) | `lib/bus/rs232/FujiBusPacket.h:76` |
| any | bad checksum/length/stalled frame: no reply | `lib/bus/rs232/rs232.cpp:114` |
| any | double opening END: command lost to the modem | `lib/bus/rs232/rs232.cpp:107` |
| any | short fixed payload accepted, rest uninitialised | `lib/bus/rs232/rs232.cpp:78` |
| unknown device | NAK with device byte `00` | |
| Fuji `FF` RESET | restarts without ACK | `lib/device/fujiDevice/fujiDevice.cpp:55` |
| Fuji `FE` GET_SSID | returns the password | `lib/device/fujiDevice/fujiDevice.cpp:438` |
| Fuji `FB` SET_SSID | failed join sends two NAKs | `lib/device/fujiDevice/fujiDevice.cpp:555` |
| Fuji `F2`/`F1` | slot names only; write-back loses paths | `lib/device/fujiDevice/fujiDevice.cpp:1575`, `:1613` |
| Fuji `E7` NEW_DISK | always NAK, after truncating the file | `lib/media/rs232/diskTypeImg.cpp:167` |
| Fuji `E0` GET_HOST_PREFIX | leftover memory | `lib/device/fujiDevice/fujiDevice.cpp:1393` |
| Fuji `E6` UNMOUNT_HOST | NAK for SD on fujinet-pc | `lib/device/fujiDevice/fujiDevice.cpp:1563` |
| Fuji `53` STATUS | always zeroes | `lib/device/rs232/rs232Fuji.cpp:61` |
| Fuji `DD` READ_APPKEY | ACK + 64 zeroes on failure | `lib/device/fujiDevice/AppKeyMixin.cpp:83` |
| Fuji `CE` | Base64 length counts a NUL | `lib/device/fujiDevice/Base64Mixin.cpp:45` |
| Disk `53` STATUS | wired to WRITE | `lib/device/rs232/disk.cpp:386` |
| Disk ROM mount | pushes to device `FF`, waits | `lib/device/rs232/disk.cpp:313` |
